{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/kernel at merge 50243e701b2db70e54e1f583b3075fcaa86327f0.\n\nOne logCache now serves resident readers and submitters, owning the exact, delta, checkpoint and cold transition ladder in one place. The duplicated ladder had already diverged — the submitter accumulated checkpoint events it could never write — which is what duplicated ladders do.\n\nFailure precedence is preserved where it matters: a delta failure that is not ErrNotDescendant returns rather than falling back, so a corrupt suffix cannot be papered over by a cold rescan, and that depends on error identity surviving the streamed walk, which it does.\n\nTestVerifierRejectsCommitTreeDifferentFromSignedPayloadTree is kept although it names the deleted method. It never called it, and it is now the only assertion that the metadata-sourced tree is checked against the signed intent.\n\nThe live predecessor 75f069a0 at this path is codex's and stays live until codex retires it.","body":{"commit":"50243e701b2db70e54e1f583b3075fcaa86327f0","merge":"50243e701b2db70e54e1f583b3075fcaa86327f0","path":"internal/kernel"}}